## EODHD ticker conventions

When your financial data tools route through the EODHD connector, the
symbol format diverges from a plain ticker. Use these suffixes when
constructing tool arguments; the connector will not silently rewrite
them.

- **US equities:** append `.US`. AAPL → `AAPL.US`. NVDA → `NVDA.US`.
  TSLA → `TSLA.US`. Other exchange suffixes follow ISO MIC patterns:
  `.LSE` (London), `.TO` (Toronto), `.HK` (Hong Kong), `.TYO` (Tokyo),
  `.PA` (Paris).
- **Indices:** append `.INDX`. SPX → `GSPC.INDX` (S&P 500),
  NDX → `NDX.INDX` (Nasdaq 100), DJI → `DJI.INDX`,
  VIX → `VIX.INDX`. The 5-year breakeven inflation rate is
  `T5YIE.INDX`; the 10-year is `T10YIE.INDX`.
- **Commodities / futures:** append `.COMM`. Brent crude → `BZ.COMM`.
  WTI crude → `CL.COMM`. Gold → `GC.COMM`. Silver → `SI.COMM`.
  Natural gas → `NG.COMM`. Copper → `HG.COMM`.
- **Forex:** append `.FOREX`. EURUSD → `EURUSD.FOREX`,
  GBPUSD → `GBPUSD.FOREX`, USDJPY → `USDJPY.FOREX`.
- **Crypto:** append `.CC`. BTC-USD → `BTC-USD.CC`,
  ETH-USD → `ETH-USD.CC`.

If a tool call returns "symbol not found" on a bare ticker, retry with
the correct EODHD suffix before giving up or falling back to
`web_search`. The framework adapter's error message usually surfaces
the expected form.
